Here is the root cause:
The original implementation of `phy_start_aneg` did not separate the locking mechanism from the core functionality of starting auto-negotiation, which could lead to issues when other functions, like `phy_ethtook_ksettings_set`, require the PHY lock. This design made it difficult to manage locking appropriately, potentially causing deadlocks or inconsistent states when multiple functions attempted to access the PHY device concurrently.

